1
00:00:00,256 --> 00:00:03,853
Under Configure, open Enable Data-at-Rest Encryption.

2
00:00:04,096 --> 00:00:08,619
Choose PE direct and enter the expected cluster UUID, PE

3
00:00:08,619 --> 00:00:11,126
endpoint and saved credential reference.

4
00:00:11,261 --> 00:00:14,944
This path uses Prism Element and an existing Local KMS;

5
00:00:14,973 --> 00:00:18,058
it does not require Prism Central or SSH.

6
00:00:18,216 --> 00:00:20,910
It is not an external key-manager conversion tool.

7
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:23,293
Keep certificate verification enabled.

8
00:00:23,437 --> 00:00:27,696
A permitted temporary exception needs an explicit reason, independent approval

9
00:00:27,832 --> 00:00:31,642
and an audit record. HTTPS remains encrypted,

10
00:00:31,714 --> 00:00:35,930
but bypassing certificate verification removes that certificate-based identity

11
00:00:35,938 --> 00:00:40,347
check. The exception applies to this operation and does not change global trust

12
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:43,731
or other workflows. Run read-only discovery.

13
00:00:43,923 --> 00:00:48,566
Verify cluster identity, complete healthy membership, supported software-encryption

14
00:00:48,660 --> 00:00:51,126
state and the reported Local KMS.

15
00:00:51,347 --> 00:00:55,870
Review licensing, platform support, other encryption tasks and key-backup

16
00:00:55,870 --> 00:01:00,314
ownership. Missing, partial or unsupported states block the operation

17
00:01:00,493 --> 00:01:02,533
rather than being converted automatically.

18
00:01:02,925 --> 00:01:06,160
Software encryption cannot be disabled after enablement.

19
00:01:06,381 --> 00:01:10,283
Review the exact plan and obtain approval from a different administrator.

20
00:01:10,532 --> 00:01:14,372
Live writes default to off until the installed version and hardware have been

21
00:01:14,372 --> 00:01:18,588
validated. In an enabled environment, the exact confirmation

22
00:01:18,724 --> 00:01:23,032
precedes fresh identity, health and state checks and one request.

23
00:01:23,436 --> 00:01:27,788
PE configuration readback and background encryption monitoring are separate from

24
00:01:27,788 --> 00:01:29,636
proof that keys can be recovered.

25
00:01:29,879 --> 00:01:33,339
Preserve and verify key backups outside the appliance.

26
00:01:33,530 --> 00:01:38,173
If submission or verification is uncertain, inspect actual PE state before

27
00:01:38,266 --> 00:01:42,857
another request. Rolling back the Orchestrator does not turn encryption off.
